```python
def find_highest_common_ancestor(root, node1, node2):
    if root is None:
        return None
    if root == node1 or root == node2:
        return root
    left_ancestor = find_highest_common_ancestor(root.left, node1, node2)
    right_ancestor = find_highest_common_ancestor(root.right, node1, node2)
    if left_ancestor and right_ancestor:
        return root
    return left_ancestor if left_ancestor else right_ancestor
```

This implementation correctly identifies the HCA by checking if the current node is one of the nodes, then recursively checking both subtrees. If both subtrees return non-null values, the current node is the HCA. If only one subtree returns a non-null value, that is the HCA. If neither does, it returns None. 

